+# Audit: the cascade (0.26.0)
+
+Date: 2026-11-03 · PR: Cochilo 0.35.0 · Auditor: Claude (graphic-design-fundamentals + impeccable)
+
+## Scope
+
+One motion token (`motion-stagger`, Cochilo) and the Cascade pattern for the Log menu: items open
+one after another from the button, on a soft arc. Motion only; no colours.
+
+## graphic-design-fundamentals (§13 checklist)
+
+| # | Question | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Brief | Pass: the menu feels like it pours out of the button, not like a grid appearing |
+| 2 | Concept | Pass: nearest the finger first, like drops |
+| 3 | Hierarchy | Pass: the order of appearance is the order of reach |
+| 4 | Contrast | Pass: unchanged |
+| 5 | Alignment and grid | Pass: end-aligned column bowed at most space3; tap targets move with the items |
+| 6 | Spacing | Pass |
+| 7 | Typography | Pass |
+| 8 | Colour | Pass |
+| 9 | Consistency | Pass: the same two durations and system easing; one new delay token |
+| 10 | Simplicity | Pass: closing stays one sink |
+| 11 | Real-size test | Pass: Cochilo's open-menu screenshots |
+| 12 | Accessibility and ergonomics | Pass: snaps with Remove animations; whole cascade under 0.6s for 8 items |
+| 13 | Production | Pass |
+
+## impeccable (audit)
+
+| # | Dimension | Score | Key finding |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Accessibility | 4 | Reduce motion honoured |
+| 2 | Performance | 4 | Graphics-layer offsets only |
+| 3 | Appearance & theming | 4 | — |
+| 4 | Platform conformance | 4 | Staggered entrance per Material motion |
+| 5 | Adaptivity | 4 | Arc in dp, same on tablets |
+| | **Total** | **20/20** | |
+
+## Asleep and awake (the timeline pattern in the same release)
+
+- **Colour:** awake has no data colour. It is a hollow ring outlined in `muted`, so event colours stay
+  data, and teal stays the one action. Passes in light, dark and night: the ring sits on `surface`,
+  and `muted` already passes there as meta text.
+- **Hierarchy:** sleep keeps leading (label role, `kind-badge-lead`); awake is body role. Entries
+  inside a stretch are set in by `space6`, a step on the spacing scale, never a literal.
+- **Reading order:** the time column shows only the stretches' starts, so it runs in order; nested
+  entries keep their time in their meta. TalkBack reads each awake stretch as a heading.
+- **Targets:** awake rows are not buttons; nested rows keep their 48dp rows and their tap to edit.
